aineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/commercial-condo-association-appraisal/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Commercial, Condo & HOA Appraisal","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Condo association insurance appraisal in Maine for boards, HOAs and business owners facing an underpaid master policy or commercial claim.","provider":{"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"State","name":"Maine"},"url":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/commercial-condo-association-appraisal/","image":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/condo-building.webp","@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/commercial-condo-association-appraisal/#service"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Can a condo board demand appraisal without a vote of all owners?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That depends on the association’s declaration and bylaws. Most boards act through a recorded board vote, but confirm authority with the association’s attorney."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does condo association insurance appraisal in Maine cover individual units?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It covers whatever the master policy insures. Unit interiors that fall under owners’ own policies are usually handled as separate claims with those carriers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can business income be part of an appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often yes, if the policy’s appraisal clause applies to the full amount of loss. It requires solid financial records and a realistic restoration timeline."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you handle mill buildings and historic structures?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Brick mill conversions, timber-framed buildings and older masonry need specialized pricing, and we build that into the scope."}}],"@id":"https://maineinsuranceappraiser.com/appraisal-work/commercial-co